()
(activity_create
 (description Implement the behavior outlined in doc/uat/activity_create.md)
 (steps
  (1 Add a click handler to the time markers in `DayView.vue`.)
  (2 In the click handler, determine the time that was clicked.)
  (3 Use the `insertActivityAtTime` action in the `activityStore` to create a new activity at the clicked time.)
  (4 Ensure that the new activity's duration is calculated correctly based on the existing activities.)
  (5 Update the UI to reflect the new activity.)
  (6 Write a test for the new behavior.)
  (7 Ensure that the activities are sorted after insertion.)
 )
)
(click_anywhere_create
 (description Allow users to create activities by clicking anywhere in the time marker area, not just on time markers.)
 (steps
  (1 Modify the click handler in `DayView.vue` to listen for clicks on the time marker container instead of the time markers.)
  (2 In the click handler, calculate the vertical position of the click within the time marker container.)
  (3 Convert the vertical position to a time in minutes, considering the height of the activity list represents 24 hours (1440 minutes).)
  (4 Use the `insertActivityAtTime` action in the `activityStore` to create a new activity at the calculated time.)
  (5 Ensure that the new activity's duration is calculated correctly based on the existing activities.)
  (6 Update the UI to reflect the new activity.)
  (7 Write a test for the new behavior.)
 )
)
